Theorem RL-15a: ArgEscaping caller-stack allocation — 4 emission categories (CRITICAL)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-15a governs ArgEscaping caller-stack allocation per Annex E §AIMS Stack Promotion: ArgEscaping values (Locality = ArgEscaping)
      SHALL be stack-allocated in the CALLER, with the header decision
      determined by the CALLEE's parameter contract (NOT the caller's
      Access, which is Owned + ArgEscaping). CRITICAL: sec-11 coexistence
      handshake + sec-04B C5 build on RL-15a; it is the Ori-novel realization
      rule whose soundness sec-04B assumed but never proved.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - The 4 distinct emission categories (the canonical enumeration per
      Annex E §AIMS RL-15a — NOT a 2x2x2 cross product; may_share
      modulates category 1 vs 2):
        (1) callee Borrowed + Unique + may_share=false -> headerless
            caller-stack (no RC ops; heap children receive field-level RcDec
            at caller scope exit per RL-14, VF-1 DecOnBorrowed exemption);
        (2) callee Borrowed + != Unique (MaybeShared/Shared), AND the
            may_share=true upgrade of category 1 -> caller-stack WITH RC
            header init MAX_REFCOUNT (immortal — the callee may emit IsShared
            per DP-4 reading the header; headerless allocation crashes;
            immortal prevents a callee RcDec freeing the stack pointer);
        (3) callee Owned -> caller-stack WITH immortal RC header (the callee
            may emit RcDec/IsShared; immortal makes a callee RcDec a no-op;
            the caller owns field cleanup);
        (4) closure-capture (PartialApply) -> TF-13 promotes Access to Owned
            only for >= HeapEscaping; CN-8 clamps Borrowed+ArgEscaping ->
            Borrowed+FunctionLocal, routing the captured variable to RL-14,
            NOT RL-15a.
    - TF-13 closure-capture exception + CN-8 Borrowed-locality-ceiling are
      explicit proof obligations (per the sec-08 RL-15a success criterion).
    - DP-8 (is_local): ArgEscaping is NOT local (it escapes into the callee),
      so RL-14/RL-15 do not apply; caller-stack promotion (RL-15a) is the
      ArgEscaping optimization.
    - Shipped: realize/project_escape.rs (escape-driven caller-stack +
      field-RcDec) + realize/decide.rs (Locality + callee-contract
      consumption).
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-8 (is_local); depends-on sec-06: IC-3
      ParamContract.access / .uniqueness / .may_share is the callee contract
      driving the category split.

  Soundness property:
    Forall caller value v with Locality(v) = ArgEscaping passed to a callee
    parameter with contract (access, uniqueness, may_share, is_closure):

      (P1) Category decision (the full 4-clause SUFFICIENT enumeration as
           explicit theorem antecedents):
        cat1: access = Borrowed AND uniqueness = Unique AND may_share = false
              -> CallerStackHeaderless
        cat1-upgrade / cat2: access = Borrowed AND (uniqueness != Unique OR
              may_share = true) -> CallerStackImmortal
        cat3: access = Owned -> CallerStackImmortal
        cat4: is_closure (PartialApply) -> routed to RL-14
              (HeaderlessStack via the CN-8 clamp), NOT RL-15a

      (P2) RC soundness per category:
        cat1: headerless is safe because the callee neither shares (may_share
              = false) nor decs (Borrowed) — no RC op touches the header;
              heap children are released by caller-scope field RcDec.
        cat2/cat3: the immortal MAX_REFCOUNT header makes every callee RcDec a
              no-op and lets a callee IsShared read a valid header, so the
              stack pointer is never freed by an RC op; the caller frame
              deallocates it; the caller owns field cleanup.
        cat4: the closure-captured variable is handled by RL-14 (the CN-8
              clamp moved it to FunctionLocal), so RL-15a's antecedent is
              never reached for it.

      (TF-13 / CN-8 obligation) No Borrowed value ever satisfies RL-15a's
        Locality = ArgEscaping antecedent: CN-8 clamps a Borrowed+ArgEscaping
        caller value to Borrowed+FunctionLocal (an Appendix-B infeasible-state
        elimination), which DP-8 marks is_local, routing it to RL-14. Hence
        "Borrowed callee parameter" in RL-15a refers to the CALLEE's contract
        for the parameter, never the value's Access at the caller (the caller
        value is Owned + ArgEscaping; the callee receives it as Borrowed).

    RL-15a refines plain ARC by stack-allocating (in the caller) values that
    escape ONLY into a callee, never to the heap — eliminating the heap
    allocation while the per-category header choice keeps every callee RC
    operation safe.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via finite enumeration
    of the 4-category callee-contract grid + the TF-13/CN-8 obligation.

    Part (P1/P2) — 4-category grid:
      cat1_borrowed_unique_no_share_headerless -> CallerStackHeaderless
      cat1_upgrade_borrowed_unique_may_share_immortal -> CallerStackImmortal
      cat2_borrowed_maybeshared_immortal -> CallerStackImmortal
      cat2_borrowed_shared_immortal -> CallerStackImmortal
      cat3_owned_immortal -> CallerStackImmortal
      cat4_closure_capture_routed_to_rl14 -> HeaderlessStack (RL-14)
      Coverage gate: 6 category cases covering all 4 canonical categories +
      the may_share category-1->2 upgrade.

    Part (TF-13 / CN-8 obligation):
      The verifier discharges cn8_clamp(Borrowed, ArgEscaping) = FunctionLocal
      AND is_local(FunctionLocal) = true — proving a Borrowed value never
      reaches RL-15a's ArgEscaping antecedent (it is always clamped to a local
      RL-14 path first). This is the Appendix-B `Borrowed ∧ ArgEscaping`
      infeasible-state elimination composed with DP-8.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl15a_argescaping_caller_stack; 4-category
        callee-contract grid + TF-13/CN-8 clamp obligation; emits Fail on a
        wrong category, a missing category, or a Borrowed-reaches-ArgEscaping
        violation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges the CRITICAL RL-15a via the full 4-category caller-stack grid (cat1 Borrowed+Unique+!may_share headerless; cat1-upgrade/cat2 Borrowed+!=Unique-or-may_share immortal; cat3 Owned immortal; cat4 closure-capture routed to RL-14) enumerated as explicit theorem antecedents, PLUS the TF-13/CN-8 obligation proving cn8_clamp(Borrowed, ArgEscaping) = FunctionLocal is_local so no Borrowed value ever reaches the ArgEscaping antecedent, grounded in the shipped realize/project_escape.rs caller-stack realization + IC-3 callee contract
